A.3 Proof of Theorem 3.1 (Distribution Condition)

Theorem 3.1. Distribution outperforms centralization under exactly matched budgets iff

G_{\text{spec}} + G_{\text{parallel}} > \mathrm{CT}^{(N)}(\mathcal{G}) + K_{\text{coord}} + \Delta_{\text{verify}} + \Delta_{\text{resource}}

Proof.

Under exactly matched budgets, \mathcal{R}(C) = \mathcal{R}(D) and \mathcal{E}(C) = \mathcal{E}(D). The performance difference is

P_D - P_C = \left[P_{\text{base}} + G_{\text{spec}} + G_{\text{parallel}} - \mathrm{CT}^{(N)} - K_{\text{coord}} - \Delta_{\text{verify}} - \Delta_{\text{resource}}\right] - P_{\text{base}}

= G_{\text{spec}} + G_{\text{parallel}} - \mathrm{CT}^{(N)} - K_{\text{coord}} - \Delta_{\text{verify}} - \Delta_{\text{resource}}

where:

· G_{\text{spec}} is the specialization gain from dividing labor among agents
· G_{\text{parallel}} is the parallelization gain from concurrent computation
· \mathrm{CT}^{(N)} is the collaboration tax (Definition 3.2)
· K_{\text{coord}} is the coordination cost (Definition 2.10)
· \Delta_{\text{verify}} is the verification overhead
· \Delta_{\text{resource}} is the compute-opportunity cost of coordination under matched budgets

Setting P_D > P_C yields the condition. \blacksquare

