A.7 Proof of Theorem 5.2 (Verification Reduces R_c)

Theorem 5.2. If verification catches fraction q of errors, then

R_c^{\text{ver}} = (1-q) R_c

Proof.

If a fraction q of propagated errors are caught and neutralized, the effective propagation probability from agent i to agent j is reduced:

p_{ij}^{\text{ver}} = (1-q) p_{ij}

Therefore:

K_{ij}^{\text{ver}} = p_{ij}^{\text{ver}} \cdot r_j = (1-q) p_{ij} r_j = (1-q) K_{ij}

The spectral radius scales linearly with matrix entries:

\rho(K^{\text{ver}}) = \rho((1-q)K) = (1-q)\rho(K) = (1-q) R_c

\blacksquare

Corollary A.7.1. Containment requires

q > 1 - \frac{1}{R_c}

Proof. For R_c^{\text{ver}} < 1:

(1-q) R_c < 1 \implies 1-q < \frac{1}{R_c} \implies q > 1 - \frac{1}{R_c}

\blacksquare

