Appendix F: Numerical Computations

F.1 Three-Agent Ring Topology

Parameters:

· N = 3
· p = 0.3 (propagation probability)
· r = 1.5 (expected errors per compromised agent)
· q = 0.5 (verification catch rate)

Signed next-generation matrix:

K = \begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0.45 & 0 \\ 0.45 & 0 & 0.45 \\ 0 & 0.45 & 0 \end{pmatrix}

Absolute-value matrix:

|K| = \begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0.45 & 0 \\ 0.45 & 0 & 0.45 \\ 0 & 0.45 & 0 \end{pmatrix}

Spectral radius:

\rho(|K|) = 0.45\sqrt{2} \approx 0.636

Verification-adjusted reproduction number:

R_c^{\text{ver}} = (1-0.5) \times 0.636 = 0.318

Expected blast radius:

\mathbb{E}[B] = \mathbf{1}^T (I - |K^{\text{ver}}|)^{-1} \mathbf{1}

Compute (I - |K^{\text{ver}}|)^{-1}:

I - |K^{\text{ver}}| = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & -0.225 & 0 \\ -0.225 & 1 & -0.225 \\ 0 & -0.225 & 1 \end{pmatrix}

The inverse is:

(I - |K^{\text{ver}}|)^{-1} = \frac{1}{\det} \begin{pmatrix} 1 - 0.0506 & 0.225 & 0.0506 \\ 0.225 & 1 & 0.225 \\ 0.0506 & 0.225 & 1 - 0.0506 \end{pmatrix}

where \det = 1 - 2(0.225)^2 = 1 - 0.10125 = 0.89875.

Therefore:

\mathbb{E}[B] = \mathbf{1}^T (I - |K^{\text{ver}}|)^{-1} \mathbf{1} \approx \frac{1 + 0.225 + 0.0506 + 0.225 + 1 + 0.225 + 0.0506 + 0.225 + 1}{0.89875}

= \frac{4.002}{0.89875} \approx 4.45

Interpretation. With verification catching 50% of errors, the effective reproduction number is R_c = 0.318 < 1, and the expected cascade size is finite and small.

F.2 Centralized Topology Comparison

Parameters:

· N = 10
· p = 0.3
· r = 1.5
· q = 0.5

Reproduction number:

R_c = N \cdot p \cdot r = 10 \times 0.3 \times 1.5 = 4.5

Verification-adjusted:

R_c^{\text{ver}} = (1-0.5) \times 4.5 = 2.25 > 1

Expected blast radius: Infinite (supercritical cascade).

Interpretation. Without sufficient verification, the centralized topology is vulnerable to catastrophic cascades. This motivates the SRVA policy, which reduced mean post-allocation R_c to 0.737.

